  "summary": "The spider is built in `recipes/spider.mjs` and imported through the bridge. `typecheck` passes and the render shows the whole spider framed from a three-quarter view with soft shadows. The render also reports motion between frames. I only looked at one still frame, so I haven't confirmed the gait visually or that the loop is seamless.\n\n- **Body:** a thorax sphere, an abdomen sphere, an abdomen marking, eyes and fangs.\n- **Legs:** eight, each with an upper segment, a knee joint and a lower segment, plus a foot.\n- **Gait:** one 2-second `walk` clip loops. Opposite-diagonal legs step together, half a cycle apart. Each leg lifts, swings forward and plants. The last key equals the first, so it should loop cleanly.\n- **Body bob:** two small up-and-down bobs per cycle, one per step, with a slight rock.\n- **Backdrop:** a large grey floor on a matching background, lit by a soft hemisphere fill and a shadow-casting key light.\n- **`src/main.ts`:** mounts the scene and sets `window.__EVAL_READY__` on the second frame. It also writes the elapsed time to `window.__TASK_STATE__`.\n\nThe legs look fairly straight and stick-like from this camera, though the knee joints are visible. Planted feet slide backward slightly during stance, because the body stays in place."
